and one can show (see \cite{GaroufalidisThurstonZickert,GaroufalidisGoernerZickert}) that these satisfy Thurston's gluing equations.
For the geometric representation of a cusped hyperbolic manifold, the shape field (field generated by the shapes) is equal to the invariant trace field, which is in general smaller than the trace field, see Maclachlan--Reid~\cite{MaclachlanReid}.
